---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const days = [
{date:"Tue 15 Dec",place:"Bangkok",title:"Arrive, check in & Chinatown",stay:"Bangkok · Night 1 of 2",morning:"Travel day: fly Dhaka to Bangkok. Compare flights into BKK and DMK; check which airport your ticket uses.",afternoon:"Check into a hostel around Old Town, Sam Yot or Chinatown. Keep plans light, get a Thai SIM/eSIM and withdraw a small amount of cash.",evening:"Walk Yaowarat Road for street food. Try a few small dishes rather than committing to a large restaurant meal.",cost:"฿500–1,200 excluding flight and bed",transport:"Airport rail/taxi depending on airport and arrival time; use official taxi queues or a reputable ride-hailing app.",book:"Book the first night near your arrival airport only if landing late; otherwise Old Town/Chinatown is more useful for sightseeing."},
{date:"Wed 16 Dec",place:"Bangkok",title:"Grand Palace, Wat Pho & river sunset",stay:"Bangkok · Night 2 of 2",morning:"Go early to the Grand Palace and Wat Phra Kaew. Dress with shoulders and knees covered; verify opening hours and ticket prices before setting out.",afternoon:"Visit Wat Pho, then take a public Chao Phraya boat to the Wat Arun area. Avoid anyone outside temples offering suspiciously cheap tours.",evening:"Watch sunset by the river and eat in Chinatown or around Tha Tien. If you're tired, skip one temple rather than rush all three.",cost:"฿900–1,800 including temple entry, boats and meals; excludes bed",transport:"Use MRT/BTS and river boats where practical; use a taxi only for awkward late-night routes.",book:"Usually possible independently. Check official temple ticket pages and opening notices."},
{date:"Thu 17 Dec",place:"Phuket",title:"Fly to Phuket & prepare for EDC",stay:"Phuket · Festival base, night 1 of 4",morning:"Take a morning flight Bangkok → Phuket if possible. Allow time for airport transfer, baggage and check-in.",afternoon:"Check into your hostel, buy water/snacks and confirm the exact EDC venue, entry rules, shuttle pickup and return plan.",evening:"Have dinner near your accommodation and get an early night. Do not assume the beach, Patong or the venue are close together in Phuket traffic.",cost:"฿1,000–2,500 excluding flight and bed",transport:"Airport bus or pre-booked/shared transfer; compare the fare and journey time to your actual hostel.",book:"Secure a refundable hostel for 17–20 Dec only after checking festival transport options."},
{date:"Fri 18 Dec",place:"Phuket · EDC",title:"EDC Thailand — day 1",stay:"Phuket · Festival base, night 2 of 4",morning:"Sleep, have a substantial breakfast and check the official festival schedule and prohibited-items list.",afternoon:"Keep the afternoon flexible. Eat before leaving, charge your phone and carry ID and ticket according to the organiser's instructions.",evening:"Festival time. Agree a meeting point with friends you make, keep your phone secure and use official transport or a prearranged ride home.",cost:"฿1,000–2,500 for food and local transport, plus ticket; excludes bed",transport:"Use the organiser's currently published shuttle/transport details if available. Confirm late-night return arrangements before entering.",book:"Official ticketing: edcthailand.frontgatetickets.com. Ticket stock, price, venue details and schedule must be checked live."},
{date:"Sat 19 Dec",place:"Phuket · EDC",title:"EDC day 2 — recovery first",stay:"Phuket · Festival base, night 3 of 4",morning:"Sleep in, rehydrate and eat a proper meal. Do not schedule an expensive early excursion after a late festival night.",afternoon:"Optional easy beach or café time close to your accommodation. Avoid a boat tour if you're exhausted or sea conditions are poor.",evening:"Return for day two. Keep a little emergency cash and a charged phone separate from your main wallet.",cost:"฿900–2,000 for food and local transport, plus ticket; excludes bed",transport:"Repeat the verified festival transport plan. Don't count on finding a cheap taxi at closing time.",book:"Check the official festival app/site for set times and venue announcements."},
{date:"Sun 20 Dec",place:"Phuket · EDC",title:"EDC day 3 & final festival night",stay:"Phuket · Festival base, night 4 of 4",morning:"Easy breakfast and a low-pressure day. Check out only if your accommodation allows luggage storage and you have a safe plan.",afternoon:"Rest, eat and charge devices. Keep the next day's transfer in mind; avoid booking a very early departure.",evening:"Enjoy the final festival night and use your planned transport back.",cost:"฿900–2,000 for food and local transport, plus ticket; excludes bed",transport:"Prearrange your return. Share your route with someone you trust.",book:"Three-day pass is usually simplest if attending all three days; confirm current availability and age/ID requirements."},
{date:"Mon 21 Dec",place:"Krabi · Ao Nang",title:"Transfer to Krabi & beach evening",stay:"Ao Nang · Night 1 of 3",morning:"Travel Phuket → Krabi by booked minivan/ferry combination or road transfer. Choose a service with clear pickup details.",afternoon:"Check into an Ao Nang hostel, walk the beach and book any island tour for the next day after checking weather.",evening:"Dinner around Ao Nang and an easy stroll. Keep valuables secure in shared accommodation.",cost:"฿1,000–2,200 including transfer, food and small expenses; excludes bed",transport:"Allow roughly 3–5 hours door-to-door depending on route, stops and traffic; verify the specific operator's schedule.",book:"Hostel around central Ao Nang is convenient for tour pickups and restaurants."},
{date:"Tue 22 Dec",place:"Krabi · Islands",title:"Four Islands or Hong Islands tour",stay:"Ao Nang · Night 2 of 3",morning:"Take a reputable group boat tour. Confirm whether national park fees, lunch, snorkel gear and hotel pickup are included.",afternoon:"Snorkel or swim only where conditions and guides say it is safe. Bring reef-safe sun protection and a dry bag.",evening:"Return, shower and eat at an Ao Nang night market or local restaurant.",cost:"฿1,500–2,800 including a group tour, park fees if applicable and meals; excludes bed",transport:"Tour pickup is easiest if your hostel is in the Ao Nang service area.",book:"Book with clear inclusions and cancellation terms; avoid promising a particular island if sea conditions change."},
{date:"Wed 23 Dec",place:"Krabi · Railay",title:"Railay Beach, viewpoints or kayaking",stay:"Ao Nang · Night 3 of 3",morning:"Take a longtail boat to Railay when the sea is suitable. Check return-boat times before walking away from the pier.",afternoon:"Choose beach time, a guided kayak or a hike only if conditions and your fitness make sense. Some viewpoints are steep and slippery.",evening:"Return to Ao Nang and prepare for the inland transfer tomorrow.",cost:"฿700–1,800 including boats, food and an optional activity; excludes bed",transport:"Longtail boats run from the Ao Nang area; schedules and fares can change with sea conditions.",book:"No need to prepay every activity; keep the day flexible for weather."},
{date:"Thu 24 Dec",place:"Khao Sok village",title:"Travel inland to the rainforest",stay:"Khao Sok village · Night 1 of 2",morning:"Take a scheduled transfer from Krabi/Ao Nang to Khao Sok. Check exact pickup point and baggage allowance.",afternoon:"Check into a village guesthouse/hostel, arrange the next day's lake trip and ask what to pack or leave behind.",evening:"Eat in the village and take a short guided night walk only with a reputable guide; wildlife sightings are never guaranteed.",cost:"฿1,200–2,800 including transfer, meals and a simple activity; excludes bed",transport:"Allow around 3–5 hours depending on service and pickup route. Confirm directly with the operator.",book:"A village stay is the budget option. Compare full lake tour packages rather than only the room price."},
{date:"Fri 25 Dec",place:"Cheow Lan Lake",title:"Lake boat trip & floating raft house",stay:"Khao Sok / lake · Night 2 of 2",morning:"Join a prearranged Cheow Lan Lake trip. Confirm whether the national park fee, boat, meals, guide and overnight room are included.",afternoon:"Enjoy the lake scenery, a guided cave or nature outing only if open and safe, and kayaking if provided.",evening:"Stay in a floating raft house if budget allows, or return to the village if using a day-trip package. Basic lake rooms can be simple and connectivity limited.",cost:"฿2,500–5,500 for an overnight package is a planning estimate; check inclusions carefully",transport:"The pier transfer is normally bundled into the tour or arranged separately. Confirm the meeting point and luggage plan.",book:"Christmas dates can sell out. Ask about room type, meals, shared/private bathroom, weather cancellation and park fees."},
{date:"Sat 26 Dec",place:"Transfer to Chiang Mai",title:"South to north — the long travel day",stay:"Chiang Mai · Night 1 of 4",morning:"Transfer from Khao Sok to Surat Thani Airport or another confirmed departure point. Keep generous buffer time.",afternoon:"Fly to Chiang Mai if a suitable connection exists; some itineraries may require a connection through Bangkok. Do not assume a direct flight operates on your date.",evening:"Check into an Old City hostel, eat nearby and rest. If flights are badly timed, consider changing the itinerary rather than risking a missed connection.",cost:"฿2,500–5,500 for transfers, flight and meals, before bed; fare varies widely",transport:"This is the itinerary's biggest logistics risk. Check actual flight schedules and transfer times before paying for the lake stay.",book:"Book the flight only after matching it to the confirmed Khao Sok checkout/transfer schedule."},
{date:"Sun 27 Dec",place:"Chiang Mai",title:"Old City temples & Doi Suthep",stay:"Chiang Mai · Night 2 of 4",morning:"Walk the Old City and visit a few temples. Dress respectfully and check entry rules at each site.",afternoon:"Visit Wat Phra That Doi Suthep if weather and time allow. Use a reputable red truck/songthaew, tour or ride-hailing option.",evening:"Explore the Sunday Walking Street market if operating on the date; otherwise choose a night market and local northern Thai food.",cost:"฿700–1,600 including local transport, meals and small entry fees; excludes bed",transport:"The Old City is walkable; Doi Suthep needs a separate uphill trip.",book:"Usually easy to arrange locally. Check the market schedule and mountain weather."},
{date:"Mon 28 Dec",place:"Chiang Mai",title:"Ethical elephant sanctuary day",stay:"Chiang Mai · Night 3 of 4",morning:"Take the sanctuary's confirmed pickup if included. Read the operator's welfare policy before paying.",afternoon:"Choose observation-led care and natural behaviour. Avoid riding, performances and forced interaction; be wary of marketing claims that cannot be substantiated.",evening:"Return to Chiang Mai, rest and have dinner near the hostel.",cost:"฿2,000–4,000 for a day visit is a planning estimate; verify transport, meals and programme inclusions",transport:"Many tours include round-trip transfer; confirm pickup zone and duration.",book:"Book directly with a transparent operator, check reviews from multiple sources and read the cancellation policy."},
{date:"Tue 29 Dec",place:"Chiang Mai · Doi Inthanon",title:"Mountain, waterfalls & park landscapes",stay:"Chiang Mai · Night 4 of 4",morning:"Join a small-group day trip or arrange a driver to Doi Inthanon National Park.",afternoon:"Visit selected waterfalls, viewpoints and permitted trails. Bring a light jacket; it can be cool at altitude.",evening:"Return to town, pack and confirm tomorrow's flight to Bangkok.",cost:"฿1,400–2,800 for a group tour or more for private transport; check park fees and lunch inclusion",transport:"A long day trip; expect several hours on the road each way depending on stops.",book:"Reserve a tour with clear pickup and park-fee inclusions, especially in the holiday period."},
{date:"Wed 30 Dec",place:"Bangkok",title:"Fly back & settle in",stay:"Bangkok · Night 1 of 5",morning:"Fly Chiang Mai → Bangkok. Choose the airport that best matches your next plans and check luggage fees.",afternoon:"Check into an Old Town, Chinatown or transit-friendly hostel. Keep your NYE route in mind.",evening:"Eat nearby and verify official New Year's Eve countdown information, access rules and transport service hours.",cost:"฿1,200–3,000 including domestic flight, transfer and food; fare varies; excludes bed",transport:"Allow buffer for airport transfers and holiday traffic.",book:"Reserve your Bangkok hostel for 30 Dec–3 Jan early; New Year dates are busy."},
{date:"Thu 31 Dec",place:"Bangkok · New Year's Eve",title:"Countdown night",stay:"Bangkok · Night 2 of 5",morning:"Sleep in, have brunch and keep daytime activities close to your base.",afternoon:"Choose one countdown venue, such as ICONSIAM or CentralWorld, only after checking the official 2026 event announcements, entry process and restrictions.",evening:"Arrive early. Set a meeting point, keep your phone charged and decide your return route before crowds build.",cost:"฿1,000–3,500 depending on food, transport and any paid event; excludes bed",transport:"Expect heavy traffic and crowded rail stations. Check official transit operating hours and don't rely on last-minute taxis.",book:"Don't buy tickets or packages from unofficial sellers. Some countdown events are free but may require registration."},
{date:"Fri 1 Jan",place:"Bangkok",title:"Recovery day & easy city exploring",stay:"Bangkok · Night 3 of 5",morning:"Sleep in and have a late breakfast. Keep this day light after New Year's Eve.",afternoon:"Choose a mall, riverside walk, massage from a reputable establishment or a café crawl.",evening:"Eat at a night market or Chinatown if open; have an early night before Ayutthaya.",cost:"฿600–1,500 excluding bed",transport:"Use MRT/BTS where operating; check holiday service notices.",book:"No need to prebook most low-key activities."},
{date:"Sat 2 Jan",place:"Ayutthaya",title:"Ancient capital day trip",stay:"Bangkok · Night 4 of 5",morning:"Take an early train or a reputable small-group tour from Bangkok. Confirm the station and departure time the day before.",afternoon:"Explore selected temple ruins. Hire a licensed local guide or use a planned route; bring water and sun protection.",evening:"Return to Bangkok and eat near your hostel.",cost:"฿900–2,200 including return transport, entry fees and meals; private tours cost more",transport:"Train plus local tuk-tuk/bicycle or a guided van. Compare total cost, not just the train ticket.",book:"Check train schedules and temple opening times close to the date."},
{date:"Sun 3 Jan",place:"Bangkok",title:"Choose your own finale",stay:"Bangkok · Night 5 of 5",morning:"Pick one: Thai cooking class, a food tour, shopping, a museum or a relaxed neighbourhood walk.",afternoon:"Leave time to pack, check in for your return flight and confirm the airport transfer.",evening:"Have a final Thai meal and keep essentials, passport and travel documents together.",cost:"฿800–2,500 depending on chosen activity; excludes bed",transport:"Choose an activity that doesn't put you far from your airport transfer route.",book:"Book a class or guided tour only after checking inclusions and cancellation terms."},
{date:"Mon 4 Jan",place:"Return to Dhaka",title:"Airport & fly home",stay:"Departure day",morning:"Check your airline's airport and check-in deadline. Leave a generous buffer for Bangkok traffic.",afternoon:"Return to Dhaka according to your flight schedule.",evening:"Keep boarding pass, passport and required travel documents accessible.",cost:"฿300–1,200 for airport transport and food; excludes flight",transport:"BKK and DMK are different airports. Verify the airport on your ticket before leaving.",book:"Confirm baggage allowance and online check-in with your airline."}
];

const stays = [
{city:"Bangkok",area:"Old Town / Chinatown",price:"฿250–800 per dorm bed/night",why:"Best for temples, street food and river access. Choose a hostel with lockers, recent reviews and a clear late check-in policy.",links:[["Hostelworld Bangkok","https://www.hostelworld.com/hostels/asia/thailand/bangkok/"],["Booking.com Bangkok","https://www.booking.com/searchresults.html?ss=Bangkok%2C+Thailand"]]},
{city:"Phuket",area:"Choose by EDC transport first",price:"฿400–1,200+ per dorm bed/night",why:"Do not book purely for Patong beach. Check the current festival venue, official shuttle pickup and late-night return. Four festival nights are worth reserving early.",links:[["Hostelworld Phuket","https://www.hostelworld.com/hostels/asia/thailand/phuket/"],["Booking.com Phuket","https://www.booking.com/searchresults.html?ss=Phuket%2C+Thailand"]]},
{city:"Krabi",area:"Central Ao Nang",price:"฿250–700 per dorm bed/night",why:"Convenient for tour pickups, restaurants and longtail boats. Check whether the hostel is within the operator's pickup zone.",links:[["Hostelworld Krabi","https://www.hostelworld.com/hostels/asia/thailand/krabi/"],["Booking.com Ao Nang","https://www.booking.com/searchresults.html?ss=Ao+Nang%2C+Krabi"]]},
{city:"Khao Sok",area:"Khao Sok village",price:"฿300–900+ for a basic bed/room",why:"Budget base for the rainforest. A lake overnight is usually a tour package, so compare the full cost including boat, meals, transfers and park fees.",links:[["Booking.com Khao Sok","https://www.booking.com/searchresults.html?ss=Khao+Sok%2C+Thailand"],["Tourism Authority of Thailand","https://www.tourismthailand.org/"]]},
{city:"Chiang Mai",area:"Old City",price:"฿250–700 per dorm bed/night",why:"Walkable temples, cafés and night markets; good base for shared tours. Check tour pickup arrangements for mountain and sanctuary days.",links:[["Hostelworld Chiang Mai","https://www.hostelworld.com/hostels/asia/thailand/chiang-mai/"],["Booking.com Chiang Mai","https://www.booking.com/searchresults.html?ss=Chiang+Mai%2C+Thailand"]]}
];

const costs = [
["Dhaka ↔ Thailand international flight","৳35,000–65,000"],
["Thai visa / entry allowance","৳0–12,000 (verify current rules)"],
["20 nights: hostels + lake stay","৳30,000–55,000"],
["Domestic flight(s)","৳12,000–28,000"],
["Ground transport & transfers","৳20,000–35,000"],
["Meals, snacks & water","৳25,000–40,000"],
["EDC ticket allowance","৳30,000–45,000"],
["Tours & activities","৳25,000–45,000"],
["SIM, insurance, laundry & incidentals","৳8,000–15,000"],
["Contingency reserve","৳25,000–35,000"]
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Thailand, Unfiltered — Zaed's Detailed Travel Plan" description="A detailed, editable 21-day Thailand itinerary with hostel areas, activity plans, booking links and estimated costs.">
<div class="nav"><div class="wrap navin"><a class="brand" href="#top">THAILAND<span>, UNFILTERED.</span></a><nav class="navlinks"><a href="#itinerary">Daily plan</a><a href="#stays">Hostels</a><a href="#budget">Budget</a><a href="#book">Booking order</a></nav><a class="btn" href="#itinerary">Start planning ↓</a></div></div>
<main id="top">
<header class="hero wrap"><div class="heroimg"><div class="herotext"><span class="eyebrow">15 DEC 2026 — 4 JAN 2027 · SOLO TRIP</span><h1>Thailand,<br><em>unfiltered.</em></h1><p>A practical, day-by-day plan for EDC Thailand, island adventures, rainforest, northern mountains, hostels and Bangkok's New Year's Eve. Costs are planning estimates until checked against live bookings.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="#itinerary">Explore the daily plan ↓</a><a class="btn ghost" href="https://edcthailand.frontgatetickets.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Official EDC tickets ↗</a></div></div></div><div class="stats"><div class="stat"><strong>21 days</strong><span>15 Dec – 4 Jan inclusive</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>20 nights</strong><span>Mostly hostel dorms</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>৳250–350k</strong><span>Target total budget</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>5 bases</strong><span>Bangkok · Phuket · Krabi · Khao Sok · Chiang Mai</span></div></div></header>

<section id="overview" class="wrap"><div class="sectionhead"><div><div class="label">Route at a glance</div><h2>Save on beds.<br/>Spend on experiences.</h2></div><p>Hostels work well for this solo trip. The two places not to cut corners are Phuket during EDC (transport matters) and the Khao Sok lake trip (compare the full package, not just the room).</p></div><div class="routegrid">
<article class="place"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1508009603885-50cf7c579365?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1000&q=85" alt="Bangkok city" loading="lazy"><div class="placebody"><div class="label">15–16 Dec · 30 Dec–3 Jan</div><h3>Bangkok</h3><p>Temples, Chinatown food, river boats, New Year's Eve and Ayutthaya day trip.</p><div class="chips"><span class="chip">Culture</span><span class="chip">Food</span><span class="chip">NYE</span></div></div></article>
<article class="place"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1589394815804-964ed0be2eb5?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1000&q=85" alt="Phuket beach" loading="lazy"><div class="placebody"><div class="label">17–20 Dec</div><h3>Phuket</h3><p>Three EDC festival days plus recovery time. Book the hostel around transport, not just beach access.</p><div class="chips"><span class="chip">EDC</span><span class="chip">Beach</span></div></div></article>
<article class="place"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1516690561799-46d8f74f9abf?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1000&q=85" alt="Krabi islands" loading="lazy"><div class="placebody"><div class="label">21–23 Dec</div><h3>Krabi</h3><p>Ao Nang base, island tour, Railay Beach and longtail boats.</p><div class="chips"><span class="chip">Islands</span><span class="chip">Kayak</span></div></div></article>
<article class="place"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1516026672322-bc52d61a55d5?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1000&q=85" alt="Tropical rainforest" loading="lazy"><div class="placebody"><div class="label">24–25 Dec</div><h3>Khao Sok</h3><p>Rainforest village and Cheow Lan Lake. Optional floating raft-house night.</p><div class="chips"><span class="chip">Jungle</span><span class="chip">Lake</span></div></div></article>
<article class="place"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1512553353614-82a7370096dc?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1000&q=85" alt="Chiang Mai temple" loading="lazy"><div class="placebody"><div class="label">26–29 Dec</div><h3>Chiang Mai</h3><p>Old City, Doi Suthep, ethical elephant sanctuary and Doi Inthanon.</p><div class="chips"><span class="chip">Culture</span><span class="chip">Mountains</span></div></div></article>
<article class="place"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1598970605070-a38a6ccd6a1d?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1000&q=85" alt="Ayutthaya ruins" loading="lazy"><div class="placebody"><div class="label">2 Jan day trip</div><h3>Ayutthaya</h3><p>Historic temple ruins on a train-based or guided day trip from Bangkok.</p><div class="chips"><span class="chip">History</span><span class="chip">Photos</span></div></div></article>
</div></section>

<section id="itinerary" class="wrap"><div class="sectionhead"><div><div class="label">The actual day-by-day plan</div><h2>What to do, when<br/>to go, what to spend.</h2></div><p>Daily costs below are per person and generally exclude accommodation unless stated. Thai baht (฿) figures are estimates; live fares, tour inclusions and opening times can change.</p></div>
<div class="timeline">{days.map((d,i)=><article class="day"><div class="date"><span>{d.date.split(" ")[0]}</span><strong>{d.date.split(" ")[1]}</strong><span>{d.date.split(" ")[2]}</span></div><div class="daycontent"><div class="daytop"><small>{d.place}</small><span class="daycount">DAY {i+1} / 21</span></div><h3>{d.title}</h3><p class="stayline">🛏 {d.stay}</p><div class="schedule"><div><b>Morning</b><p>{d.morning}</p></div><div><b>Afternoon</b><p>{d.afternoon}</p></div><div><b>Evening</b><p>{d.evening}</p></div></div><div class="detailrow"><b>Estimated spend</b><span>{d.cost}</span></div><div class="detailrow"><b>Getting around</b><span>{d.transport}</span></div><div class="booktip"><b>Booking tip</b><p>{d.book}</p></div></div></article>)}</div></section>

<section id="stays" class="wrap"><div class="sectionhead"><div><div class="label">Where to sleep</div><h2>Hostel-first accommodation.</h2></div><p>Use these neighbourhoods and comparison links to find current inventory for your exact dates. These are price guides, not live quotes or a guarantee of availability.</p></div><div class="staygrid">{stays.map(s=><article class="staycard"><div class="stayhead"><span class="label">{s.city}</span><span class="price">{s.price}</span></div><h3>{s.area}</h3><p>{s.why}</p><div class="linklist">{s.links.map(l=><a href={l[1]} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">{l[0]} ↗</a>)}</div></article>)}</div><div class="safety"><b>Hostel booking checklist</b><p>Check recent reviews, air-conditioning, locker availability, location on a map, late check-in, cancellation deadline, taxes and whether the displayed price is per person or per room. Compare the final total for every date, especially 18–20 December and 30–31 December.</p></div></section>

<section id="experiences" class="wrap"><div class="sectionhead"><div><div class="label">Activity cost guide</div><h2>Pick the experiences<br/>that matter most.</h2></div><p>These ranges are budget placeholders. Confirm what is included before booking, especially park fees, transport, meals and equipment.</p></div><div class="activitygrid">
<article class="activity"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1470229722913-7c0e2dbbafd3?auto=format&fit=crop&w=900&q=85" alt="Electronic music festival" loading="lazy"><div class="inside"><h3>EDC Thailand · 18–20 Dec</h3><p>Buy via official ticketing. Check age, ID, entry, bag policy, venue and transport notices. A hostel far away can cost more once transfers are added.</p><span class="price">Budget allowance: ৳30,000–45,000 for ticket</span><p><a href="https://edcthailand.frontgatetickets.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Official ticket checkout ↗</a> · <a href="https://thailand.edc.com/en/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Festival info ↗</a></p></div></article>
<article class="activity"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1540541338287-41700207dee6?auto=format&fit=crop&w=900&q=85" alt="Tropical sea" loading="lazy"><div class="inside"><h3>Krabi island tour</h3><p>Group Four Islands/Hong Islands tour. Confirm park fees, lunch, snorkel gear, pickup and weather cancellation.</p><span class="price">฿1,500–2,800</span></div></article>
<article class="activity"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1500530855697-b586d89ba3ee?auto=format&fit=crop&w=900&q=85" alt="Mountain landscape" loading="lazy"><div class="inside"><h3>Cheow Lan Lake</h3><p>Compare village-based day trips with overnight floating raft-house packages; verify all meals and transfers.</p><span class="price">฿2,500–5,500 for overnight package (estimate)</span></div></article>
<article class="activity"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1552550049-db0e9b6b6a3f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=900&q=85" alt="Elephant in habitat" loading="lazy"><div class="inside"><h3>Elephant sanctuary</h3><p>Choose welfare-led observation and natural behaviour. Avoid riding, shows and forced bathing/handling.</p><span class="price">฿2,000–4,000 for day visit (estimate)</span></div></article>
<article class="activity"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1512553353614-82a7370096dc?auto=format&fit=crop&w=900&q=85" alt="Northern Thai temple" loading="lazy"><div class="inside"><h3>Doi Suthep & Doi Inthanon</h3><p>Use a shared tour or compare driver costs. Ask if park fees, lunch and hotel pickup are included.</p><span class="price">Doi Inthanon group tour: ฿1,400–2,800 (estimate)</span></div></article>
<article class="activity"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1555939594-58d7cb561ad1?auto=format&fit=crop&w=900&q=85" alt="Thai food" loading="lazy"><div class="inside"><h3>Food, markets & cooking</h3><p>Mix street food with a cooking class or guided food walk. Keep a little extra for coffee and snacks on travel days.</p><span class="price">Meals: roughly ฿350–700/day</span></div></article>
</div><div class="safety"><b>Wildlife safety</b><p>Avoid tiger-contact photo attractions. Close contact with large predators carries real risk and raises animal-welfare concerns. For wildlife, prefer reputable observation-led experiences.</p></div></section>

<section id="budget" class="wrap"><div class="sectionhead"><div><div class="label">Full trip budget</div><h2>Will ৳250–350k cover it?</h2></div><p>It may, with hostel dorms and careful choices, but the upper end is safer if your flights, EDC pass or lake tour cost more than expected.</p></div><div class="budget"><div class="budgethero"><div class="label">Target</div><div class="amount">৳250–350k</div><p>Build your budget from live quotes. Christmas and New Year's Eve rates can be significantly higher; keep the contingency reserve untouched until needed.</p><a class="btn" href="https://www.hostelworld.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Compare hostel prices ↗</a></div><div class="budgetlist">{costs.map(c=><div class="budgetrow"><span>{c[0]}</span><span>{c[1]}</span></div>)}<p class="note">All amounts are estimates, not quotes; ranges overlap and the high end may exceed ৳350,000. Do not double-count the EDC allowance if your chosen ticket is included elsewhere. Check current visa requirements for Bangladeshi passport holders with official sources.</p></div></div><div class="costtips"><div><b>Save here</b><p>Hostel dorms, street food, MRT/BTS, shared tours, and booking domestic transport after checking baggage rules.</p></div><div><b>Don't underbudget</b><p>EDC ticket and late-night transfers, the 26 Dec south-to-north connection, travel insurance, and the lake overnight package.</p></div><div><b>Keep flexible</b><p>Boat trips depend on weather. Don't prepay non-refundable activities that rely on sea conditions or tight flight connections.</p></div></div></section>

<section id="book" class="wrap"><div class="sectionhead"><div><div class="label">Booking order</div><h2>What to reserve first.</h2></div><p>Work through this list in order. Open links in a new tab and save confirmation numbers in one place.</p></div><div class="booksteps">
<div class="step"><span>01</span><div><h3>EDC ticket</h3><p>Check live ticket tier, availability, age/ID rules, venue and official transport information.</p><a href="https://edcthailand.frontgatetickets.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Official ticket checkout ↗</a></div></div>
<div class="step"><span>02</span><div><h3>International flights</h3><p>Compare Dhaka → Bangkok and return on 4 Jan. Check baggage, airport (BKK/DMK) and arrival time.</p><a href="https://www.google.com/travel/flights" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Compare flights ↗</a></div></div>
<div class="step"><span>03</span><div><h3>Phuket hostel and EDC transport</h3><p>Book 17–20 Dec with a refundable rate if possible, after confirming where the official shuttle picks up.</p><a href="https://www.hostelworld.com/hostels/asia/thailand/phuket/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Find Phuket hostels ↗</a></div></div>
<div class="step"><span>04</span><div><h3>Bangkok New Year's stay</h3><p>Reserve 30 Dec–3 Jan early; choose a location that makes your countdown return practical.</p><a href="https://www.hostelworld.com/hostels/asia/thailand/bangkok/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Find Bangkok hostels ↗</a></div></div>
